(modprobe xeno_native?)

The mistake that I did was giving  explicitly optional CFLAGS for 32bit whi=
le configuring Xenomai, after upgrading the Kerenel.
While my kernel and CentOS is 64 bit.
I just did as per README.INSTALL of xenomai, where I did not consider not t=
o give those options while configuring Xenomai.

$xenomai_root/configure --enable-x86-sep --enable-smp --host=3Di686-linux C=
FLAGS=3D"-m32 -O2" LDFLAGS=3D"-m32"
The above configures to make 32bit libraries of Xenomai. Libraries are buil=
t successfuly and could instal but while running for example "latency" we s=
ee modprobe error.

Now I tried as
>/usr/src/xenomai/configure --enable-x86-sep --enable-smp
The above configures to make dependent on OS(I think) it configured to make=
 for 64 bit libraries of Xenomai.

> make clean    /* I HAVE TO DO this, otherwise compilation /linker error s=
aying librtdk_la-init.o not found */
> make
> make isntall /* as root */

I have one question is that not possible to run 32bit Xenomai libraries tha=
t runs on 64bit OS ? Or Sorry if it is a wrong question ?

Thanks for your time.  Hope this may help BONOS Antonis, if he still did no=
t get solution yet.
